1
00:00:01,550 --> 00:00:04,408
Day five of the
zombie apocalypse.

2
00:00:04,408 --> 00:00:06,137
You've survived
the riots.

3
00:00:06,137 --> 00:00:08,098
You've survived
the infected.

4
00:00:08,098 --> 00:00:09,445
You've even
survived your

5
00:00:09,445 --> 00:00:10,713
neighbor Gary.

6
00:00:10,713 --> 00:00:12,640
Which,
statistically speaking,

7
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,650
should've been
impossible.

8
00:00:14,650 --> 00:00:16,947
But there's one
tiny problem.

9
00:00:16,947 --> 00:00:18,944
You've been
bitten.

10
00:00:20,230 --> 00:00:23,164
Oh, you've gotta
be kidding me.

11
00:00:23,966 --> 00:00:26,184
Hiiii! It's Gary!

12
00:00:26,184 --> 00:00:28,427
And the guy
outside your door?

13
00:00:28,427 --> 00:00:30,877
He got bitten
four days ago.

14
00:00:30,877 --> 00:00:31,852
Yeah.

15
00:00:31,852 --> 00:00:33,013
We should
probably start at

16
00:00:33,013 --> 00:00:34,592
the beginning.

17
00:00:36,542 --> 00:00:37,764
Day one.

18
00:00:37,764 --> 00:00:39,134
The government
tells everyone

19
00:00:39,134 --> 00:00:41,083
to stay indoors.

20
00:00:41,083 --> 00:00:43,463
So naturally,
the entire city

21
00:00:43,463 --> 00:00:45,773
decides to
go shopping.

22
00:00:45,825 --> 00:00:47,123
That doesn't
look good.

23
00:00:47,123 --> 00:00:48,029
Correct.

24
00:00:48,029 --> 00:00:49,875
For once,
your two remaining

25
00:00:49,875 --> 00:00:51,384
brain cells
are working

26
00:00:51,384 --> 00:00:52,835
together.

27
00:00:53,485 --> 00:00:55,052
Unfortunately,
you've got

28
00:00:55,052 --> 00:00:56,295
enough food
to survive

29
00:00:56,295 --> 00:00:58,788
approximately
eleven minutes.

30
00:00:58,788 --> 00:01:00,698
...Great.

31
00:01:01,948 --> 00:01:03,852
Welcome to the
supermarket.

32
00:01:03,852 --> 00:01:05,803
Humanity's final
demonstration

33
00:01:05,803 --> 00:01:07,449
of common sense.

34
00:01:07,449 --> 00:01:10,746
Water. Canned food.
Batteries.

35
00:01:10,746 --> 00:01:11,791
And something
to defend

36
00:01:11,791 --> 00:01:13,329
yourself with.

37
00:01:13,329 --> 00:01:14,223
Good.

38
00:01:14,223 --> 00:01:16,415
You're doing
surprisingly well.

39
00:01:16,415 --> 00:01:18,148
Wait. What's that?

40
00:01:18,148 --> 00:01:20,052
...A rubber duck?

41
00:01:21,210 --> 00:01:23,242
He looked lonely.

42
00:01:23,242 --> 00:01:24,275
Of course.

43
00:01:24,275 --> 00:01:25,982
Emotional
support duck.

44
00:01:25,982 --> 00:01:27,143
Very important
during the

45
00:01:27,143 --> 00:01:29,558
collapse of
civilization.

46
00:01:30,772 --> 00:01:31,928
Gary?

47
00:01:31,928 --> 00:01:33,424
Hiiii!

48
00:01:33,424 --> 00:01:35,698
You seen the
sugar aisle?

49
00:01:36,348 --> 00:01:37,439
You know what?

50
00:01:37,439 --> 00:01:39,181
Shopping's over.

51
00:01:44,731 --> 00:01:47,633
Day two.
The internet is dead.

52
00:01:47,633 --> 00:01:49,363
The streets
are empty.

53
00:01:49,363 --> 00:01:50,478
And somebody's
knocking on

54
00:01:50,478 --> 00:01:51,778
your door at
three in the

55
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:52,786
morning.

56
00:01:52,786 --> 00:01:54,156
Which is rude.

57
00:01:54,156 --> 00:01:56,730
Even by apocalypse
standards.

58
00:01:56,730 --> 00:01:59,770
Hiii! It's Gary.
From 4B.

59
00:01:59,770 --> 00:02:03,370
Can I borrow
some... sugar?

60
00:02:03,370 --> 00:02:05,532
Gary does not
need sugar.

61
00:02:05,532 --> 00:02:08,038
Just a little?

62
00:02:09,308 --> 00:02:10,588
Nope.

63
00:02:10,588 --> 00:02:13,351
A locked door.
A baseball bat.

64
00:02:13,351 --> 00:02:14,640
And a chair.

65
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:16,277
The three
pillars of modern

66
00:02:16,277 --> 00:02:18,204
home security.

67
00:02:19,426 --> 00:02:21,924
I can hear
you breathing.

68
00:02:22,054 --> 00:02:23,564
...What?

69
00:02:25,962 --> 00:02:28,064
See you tomorrow!

70
00:02:29,105 --> 00:02:30,164
Tomorrow?!

71
00:02:32,914 --> 00:02:34,470
Day three.

72
00:02:34,470 --> 00:02:36,548
You've learned
two things.

73
00:02:36,548 --> 00:02:38,510
Don't trust
your neighbors.

74
00:02:38,510 --> 00:02:39,868
And never trust
anyone who

75
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:41,900
smiles that much
while asking

76
00:02:41,900 --> 00:02:43,206
for sugar.

77
00:02:43,206 --> 00:02:45,087
Unfortunately,
things are

78
00:02:45,087 --> 00:02:46,573
getting worse.

79
00:02:46,573 --> 00:02:48,280
Because the
infection isn't

80
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:50,193
just affecting
people.

81
00:02:50,193 --> 00:02:51,842
Rats. Pigeons.

82
00:02:51,842 --> 00:02:54,047
Even your
adorable little-

83
00:02:54,708 --> 00:02:57,907
Mister Whiskers?

84
00:02:58,237 --> 00:03:00,577
Hey, buddy...

85
00:03:00,577 --> 00:03:01,481
Oh.

86
00:03:01,481 --> 00:03:03,072
Mister Whiskers
has chosen

87
00:03:03,072 --> 00:03:04,546
violence.

88
00:03:06,556 --> 00:03:08,446
AAAAAH!

89
00:03:09,296 --> 00:03:10,968
Wait a minute.

90
00:03:12,618 --> 00:03:13,744
Against all
reasonable

91
00:03:13,744 --> 00:03:15,137
expectations...

92
00:03:15,137 --> 00:03:16,865
the duck
was useful.

93
00:03:16,865 --> 00:03:18,351
Congratulations.

94
00:03:18,351 --> 00:03:19,698
You've lost your
apartment to

95
00:03:19,698 --> 00:03:21,927
a nine-pound cat.

96
00:03:21,945 --> 00:03:22,781
...At least I've
still got the

97
00:03:22,781 --> 00:03:24,887
duck.

98
00:03:30,137 --> 00:03:31,391
Day four.

99
00:03:31,391 --> 00:03:33,817
Your apartment
belongs to the cat.

100
00:03:33,817 --> 00:03:35,245
The streets
belong to the

101
00:03:35,245 --> 00:03:36,325
infected.

102
00:03:36,325 --> 00:03:37,765
And your building
apparently

103
00:03:37,765 --> 00:03:39,423
belongs to Gary.

104
00:03:39,423 --> 00:03:41,273
You've gotta
be kidding me.

105
00:03:41,273 --> 00:03:43,270
You need
somewhere safer.

106
00:03:43,270 --> 00:03:44,744
Fewer entrances.

107
00:03:44,744 --> 00:03:46,962
A clear view of
the surroundings.

108
00:03:46,962 --> 00:03:49,864
And preferably
no cats.

109
00:03:51,114 --> 00:03:52,971
Something's
coming.

110
00:03:54,421 --> 00:03:56,797
Good news.
You can still run.

111
00:03:56,797 --> 00:03:59,490
Bad news.
So can they.

112
00:04:01,540 --> 00:04:04,164
For the first time
in four days...

113
00:04:04,164 --> 00:04:05,511
you can actually
see what's

114
00:04:05,511 --> 00:04:06,723
happening.

115
00:04:06,723 --> 00:04:07,605
Okay.

116
00:04:07,605 --> 00:04:08,975
Maybe don't
stand that close

117
00:04:08,975 --> 00:04:10,181
to the edge.

118
00:04:10,181 --> 00:04:11,679
One can of food.

119
00:04:11,679 --> 00:04:13,397
Half a bottle
of water.

120
00:04:13,397 --> 00:04:15,104
And batteries
for a flashlight

121
00:04:15,104 --> 00:04:16,803
you forgot
to bring.

122
00:04:16,803 --> 00:04:18,188
...Seriously?

123
00:04:19,138 --> 00:04:21,193
...survivors...
evacuation...

124
00:04:21,193 --> 00:04:22,331
parking garage...

125
00:04:22,331 --> 00:04:23,757
tomorrow
morning...

126
00:04:23,757 --> 00:04:25,173
An evacuation?

127
00:04:25,173 --> 00:04:27,321
Tomorrow morning?
Well.

128
00:04:27,321 --> 00:04:29,550
That's either
incredibly lucky...

129
00:04:29,550 --> 00:04:31,443
or the worst
idea anyone's had

130
00:04:31,443 --> 00:04:32,741
all week.

131
00:04:32,741 --> 00:04:34,413
...do not
approach anyone

132
00:04:34,413 --> 00:04:36,317
showing signs
of infection...

133
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:39,150
especially unusual
behavior...

134
00:04:39,233 --> 00:04:40,720
Helloooo?

135
00:04:40,720 --> 00:04:43,135
Gary. Of course
it's Gary.

136
00:04:50,485 --> 00:04:53,411
Day five. Your
water is gone.

137
00:04:53,411 --> 00:04:55,814
Your food is
almost gone.

138
00:04:55,814 --> 00:04:57,010
But there's
an evacuation

139
00:04:57,010 --> 00:04:59,098
point a few
blocks away.

140
00:04:59,098 --> 00:05:00,549
All you have
to do...

141
00:05:00,549 --> 00:05:02,813
is get out of
the building.

142
00:05:02,894 --> 00:05:05,103
Mister Whiskers?!

143
00:05:05,103 --> 00:05:07,378
Oh, for crying
out loud.

144
00:05:07,575 --> 00:05:09,548
We can talk
about this.

145
00:05:09,548 --> 00:05:11,313
No, you can't.

146
00:05:13,223 --> 00:05:15,113
AAAAAH!

147
00:05:15,963 --> 00:05:17,803
Oh. That's bad.

148
00:05:17,803 --> 00:05:19,823
Your entire
first aid kit...

149
00:05:19,823 --> 00:05:22,910
is one unicorn
band-aid.

150
00:05:22,910 --> 00:05:24,660
You've gotta
be kidding me.

151
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:26,367
That is
not a cure.

152
00:05:26,367 --> 00:05:27,783
But at least the
unicorn looks

153
00:05:27,783 --> 00:05:29,350
confident.

154
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:33,590
Hello?!
Is anybody up there?!

155
00:05:33,770 --> 00:05:35,620
Please!
I need help!

156
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:37,663
Now you've
got a problem.

157
00:05:37,663 --> 00:05:39,602
Someone needs
your help.

158
00:05:39,602 --> 00:05:40,949
But if that
bite means what

159
00:05:40,949 --> 00:05:42,586
you think
it means...

160
00:05:42,586 --> 00:05:43,550
you might
be the most

161
00:05:43,550 --> 00:05:44,722
dangerous
thing in this

162
00:05:44,722 --> 00:05:46,162
building.

163
00:05:46,288 --> 00:05:48,302
Hey! Up here!

164
00:05:49,152 --> 00:05:50,893
You need a
distraction.

165
00:05:50,893 --> 00:05:52,089
Something loud.

166
00:05:52,089 --> 00:05:54,910
Something completely
ridiculous.

167
00:05:55,273 --> 00:05:57,450
I knew you'd
come in handy.

168
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,735
Unbelievable.

169
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:02,094
The duck has
now saved your

170
00:06:02,094 --> 00:06:03,812
life twice.

171
00:06:06,462 --> 00:06:08,842
Thank you.
Seriously.

172
00:06:08,842 --> 00:06:10,882
You saved my life.

173
00:06:10,882 --> 00:06:12,062
Yeah. No problem.

174
00:06:12,062 --> 00:06:12,494
Wait.

175
00:06:12,494 --> 00:06:14,492
What happened
to your arm?

176
00:06:14,492 --> 00:06:15,261
Nothing.

177
00:06:15,261 --> 00:06:16,462
Is that a bite?

178
00:06:16,462 --> 00:06:17,362
...No?

179
00:06:17,362 --> 00:06:20,044
Excellent.
Very convincing.

180
00:06:20,044 --> 00:06:21,751
You should
consider a career

181
00:06:21,751 --> 00:06:23,401
in politics.

182
00:06:23,401 --> 00:06:24,988
You were bitten?!

183
00:06:24,988 --> 00:06:26,769
It was a cat!

184
00:06:26,769 --> 00:06:28,411
That's worse!

185
00:06:29,613 --> 00:06:32,031
Hiiii! It's Gary!

186
00:06:32,448 --> 00:06:35,811
Oh, not this
guy again.

187
00:06:35,811 --> 00:06:37,241
You know him?

188
00:06:37,241 --> 00:06:38,611
Unfortunately.

189
00:06:38,793 --> 00:06:40,981
Hey! You got
bitten too?

190
00:06:40,981 --> 00:06:42,141
...Too?

191
00:06:42,141 --> 00:06:44,661
Yeah. Day one.

192
00:06:44,661 --> 00:06:45,450
Wait.

193
00:06:45,450 --> 00:06:47,494
Gary got bitten
on day one.

194
00:06:47,494 --> 00:06:49,235
That was four
days ago.

195
00:06:49,235 --> 00:06:51,238
And he's
still talking.

196
00:06:51,238 --> 00:06:54,128
Gary? How are
you still alive?

197
00:06:54,585 --> 00:06:56,858
Funny you
should ask.

198
00:06:56,858 --> 00:06:58,598
You wanna know
something?

199
00:06:58,598 --> 00:07:00,062
I don't think
we're turning

200
00:07:00,062 --> 00:07:02,088
into the
same thing.

201
00:07:04,838 --> 00:07:06,301
Congratulations.

202
00:07:06,301 --> 00:07:08,960
You survived your
first five days.

203
00:07:08,960 --> 00:07:10,840
Now you just have
to survive...

204
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:12,622
whatever
comes next.

205
00:07:12,622 --> 00:07:15,037
...evacuation...
noon...

206
00:07:15,037 --> 00:07:17,266
parking garage...
